# iTerm2 menu shortcuts installers/iterm2 sets in NSUserKeyEquivalents, one
# per line: exact menu title|key. In the key, @ is cmd, ^ ctrl, ~ opt, $ shift;
# ↩ is return and ← → ↑ ↓ the arrows, written as the characters themselves. A menu
# shortcut set here replaces the item's default, so cmd+d and cmd+shift+d no
# longer split, and cmd+ctrl+arrows no longer move the divider.
Split Vertically with Current Profile|@↩
Split Horizontally with Current Profile|@$↩
Maximize Active Pane|@~↩
Toggle Full Screen|@^f
Move Divider Left|^~←
Move Divider Right|^~→
Move Divider Up|^~↑
Move Divider Down|^~↓
Select Pane Left|@^←
Select Pane Right|@^→
Select Pane Above|@^↑
Select Pane Below|@^↓
Open Quickly|@$a
Select Output of Last Command|@$o
